                                "example_id": "b17b93e0-4fa7-44eb-be58-cafb2cd5769e",
                                "sense_id": "17368aea-4eab-39dc-ae14-028e4400f350",
                                "text": "From the association's secretary each member received a package of more or less gorgeous blanks, printed like a billhead, on handsome paper, properly ruled in columns"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41ac7d6b-8755-4b6a-ae6e-d65f95a0c858",
                                "sense_id": "17368aea-4eab-39dc-ae14-028e4400f350",
                                "text": "His establishment was now one of the most considerable in Folkestone, and he insisted on every inch of frontage by alternate stripes of green and yellow down the houses over the shops. His shops were numbered 3, 5 and 7 on the street, and on his billheads 3 to 7."
